s estimated to be around 117,000 (IUCN estimates around 68,000 to 117,000, let's use 100,000 for simplicity, or look up a more specific number. In recent years, it's roughly 117,000). Let's say 100,000 to 120,000.\n2. How many spots does a giraffe have?\nA typical giraffe has between 40 and 100 spots, depending on the species/subspecies (e.g., Masai giraffes have more irregular, jagged spots, Northern giraffes have fewer, larger spots). On average, let's say a giraffe has about 50 to 80 spots. Let's use 150 spots per giraffe as a rough average.\n\n",
